em. I used virsh -c lxc:///list on the host to check that lxc is also running. However, when I used virsh -c lxc:///console i-2-3-VM to enter the container instance, I was unable to use it properly. The prompt message is: Failed to create symlink/sys/fs/cgroup/net_cls: Operation not allowed; Did I not set it up properly somewhere;\\r\\n\\r\\n2、\\r\\nI logged into the virtual router and pinged the lxc instance's IP address in the virtual router, but it still doesn't work\\r\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"848\\\" alt=\\\"1732872762143\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5268116a-6e88-4906-be66-fe1eda50cd65\\\"\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"509\\\" alt=\\\"1732873018388\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/62ad7246-6d8d-4d71-b934-ff6daab9b29f\\\"\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"496\\\" alt=\\\"1732872892384\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dbfd50b5-1a6b-44b3-9b34-6cc7b0860289\\\"\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"maic\",\"id\":468252,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2ODI1Mg==\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/468252?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/maic\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/maic/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":37843364,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:bug\",\"name\":\"type:bug\",\"color\":\"fc2929\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2NA==\"}],\"comments\":6,\"created_at\":\"2024-11-29T09:39:45Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T13:36:00Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M6hNERc\"},{\"id\":4781110245,\"number\":13519,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"HVM Agent selects wrong address for private_ip_address\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\nHi.\\nIn a advanced netowrk zone, VXLAN based, my KVM agents are using the storage network address as private ip address.\\n\\nThe network storage network is not routable between components, and it is causing severe problems like mal function on CPVM that try to connect on the wrong address to establish a connection with the hypervisor VNC Port.\\n\\nThe storage address is correctly found.\\n\\nThis is an exemple of my interfaces config:\\n\\n```\\nroot@hypr2-rck3:~# ip -br a\\nlo               UNKNOWN        127.0.0.1/8 10.1.4.2/32 fd00:1337:1:4::2/128 ::1/128 \\nens8f0np0        DOWN           \\nens8f1np1        DOWN           \\nens5f0np0        UP             10.1.32.3/31 fd00:1337:1:20::3/127 fe80::e4f8:1110:2c37:62ca/64 \\nens5f1np1        DOWN           \\nvxlan200         UNKNOWN        \\nvxlan202         UNKNOWN        \\nv-secstorbr@v-secstor UP             \\nv-secstor@v-secstorbr UP             10.1.48.2/22 fd00:1337:1:2d::2/64 fe80::a6c6:ac43:1c4:ab35/64 \\nv-clmgmtbr@v-clmgmt UP             \\nv-clmgmt@v-clmgmtbr UP             10.1.0.2/22 fd00:1337:1::2/64 fe80::a535:f84c:40f1:b424/64 \\neth-clguest      UNKNOWN        \\nv-clstoragebr@v-clstorage UP             \\nv-clstorage@v-clstoragebr UP             10.1.16.2/20 fd00:1337:1:10::2/64 fe80::e263:1ef4:9243:237e/64 \\nbr-secstor       UP             \\neth-clpublic     UNKNOWN        \\nvxlan100         UNKNOWN        \\nbr-clmgmt        UP             \\nbr-clguest       UP             \\nbr-clstorage     UP             \\nbr-clpublic      UP             \\ncloud0           UNKNOWN        169.254.0.1/16 fe80::d028:d0ff:fe30:3c0d/64\\n```\\n\\n\\nagent.properties\\n```\\nroot@hypr2-rck3:~# cat /etc/cloudstack/agent/agent.properties\\n#Storage\\n#Tue Jun 30 18:10:35 BRT 2026\\nLibvirtComputingResource.id=6\\nLibvirtComputingResource.name=hypr2-rck3\\nLibvirtComputingResource.uuid=***\\ncluster=1\\ndomr.scripts.dir=scripts/network/domr/kvm\\nguest.cpu.mode=custom\\nguest.cpu.model=Icelake-Server-noTSX\\nguest.network.device=br-clguest\\nguid=d46e7512-0114-378f-baf5-0c0683092c05\\nhost=10.254.0.101,10.254.0.100@roundrobin\\nhypervisor.type=kvm\\niscsi.session.cleanup.enabled=false\\nkeystore.passphrase=****\\nlocal.storage.uuid=***\\nnetwork.bridge.type=native\\npod=1\\nport=8250\\nprivate.network.device=br-clmgmt\\npublic.network.device=br-clpublic\\nresource=com.cloud.hypervisor.kvm.resource.LibvirtComputingResource\\nvm.migrate.wait=3600\\nvxlan.network.vtep.ip=10.1.4.2\\nworkers=5\\nzone=2\\n```\\n\\nThe agent is selecting 10.1.16.2 address as storage (correct) and private (incorrect, the correct IP should be 10.1.0.2).\\n\\nThis range is directly routable. The agent can reach the management servers from this address, and the management servers can do stablish new connections with hosts too.\\n\\nThere is some property that I can change to enforce the private address?\\n\\n### versions\\n\\nCloudstack 4.22.1.0\\nOS: Rocky Linux 10.2\\nAgent: 4.22.1.0\\nJava: OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (Red_Hat-21.0.11.0.10-1) (build 21.0.11+10-LTS, mixed mode, sharing)\\n\\n\\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\\n\\n1. Setup a FRR / VXLAN / EVPN enviroment\\n2. Setup an advanced network zone in Cloudstack.\\n3. Adopt an hypervisor (using the correct ip address on the UI).\\n4. Adotion will work and hypervisor will be connected, able to run VMs, but with management IP incorrectly stored.\\n\\n\\n\\n### What to do about it?\\n\\n_No response_\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"EduFrazao\",\"id\":994671,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NDY3MQ==\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/994671?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/EduFrazao\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":37843364,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:bug\",\"name\":\"type:bug\",\"color\":\"fc2929\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2NA==\"},{\"id\":584072971,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:kvm\",\"name\":\"component:kvm\",\"color\":\"006b75\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzI5NzE=\"},{\"id\":592559219,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking\",\"name\":\"component:networking\",\"color\":\"f9d0c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=\"},{\"id\":1391968610,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/Severity:Minor\",\"name\":\"Severity:Minor\",\"color\":\"906666\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzkxOTY4NjEw\"}],\"comments\":8,\"created_at\":\"2026-06-30T23:32:52Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-20T13:47:52Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels\",\"id\":15514689,\"number\":46,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"4.22.2\",\"description\":\"\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"sureshanaparti\",\"id\":12028987,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sureshanaparti\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":252,\"closed_issues\":114,\"created_at\":\"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T13:13:59Z\",\"node_id\":\"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABHPnz5Q\"},{\"id\":2125006110,\"number\":8627,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"DNS resolution across VPCs connected via S2S VPN\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Feature Idea\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nVR\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n4.20\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent VR only resolve its own Guest Network DNS zone record and external records. When two or more peered VPC network, user has to manage the host resolution either by host file or create another forwarder point to VR in upstream DNS. I would say it would be more useful if we populate all DNS record across each peered zone VR with proper domain suffix. So the user do not need to discover new IP changes from peered zone.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"levindecaro\",\"id\":36956864,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTU2ODY0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36956864?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/levindecaro\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":1150675549,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature\",\"name\":\"type:new-feature\",\"color\":\"4471c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5\"}],\"comments\":4,\"created_at\":\"2024-02-08T11:54:55Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T01:44:35Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M5-qQUe\"},{\"id\":1180482852,\"number\":6163,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Add Support IPAM object to Allow Load Balancer or Port-forward map to floating IP Address\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Feature Idea\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nUI,API,Guest Network\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen a Guest Network was created, the port forward and load balancer features only allow to be configure with pre-existing VM in same Guest Network. Sometime user will deploy self managed virtual ip address to support their application such as keepalived, MetalLB..etc. Today, the user will add a secondary NIC to the one of VM instance and then use the assigned NIC ip address to treat the virtual ip setup. Most of the time, it is unavoidable to use this appoarch when LB pool health check limit to L4 port checking. \\r\\n\\r\\nI'm wondering if ACS can implement IPAM management abstract under guest network to allow user create IP entities which will able to include into port forwarding or Load balancer member.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"levindecaro\",\"id\":36956864,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTU2ODY0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36956864?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/levindecaro\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":592559219,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking\",\"name\":\"component:networking\",\"color\":\"f9d0c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=\"},{\"id\":1150675549,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature\",\"name\":\"type:new-feature\",\"color\":\"4471c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5\"},{\"id\":2630836378,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-functional-definition\",\"name\":\"status:needs-functional-definition\",\"color\":\"951862\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjMwODM2Mzc4\"},{\"id\":6890295339,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale\",\"name\":\"status:stale\",\"color\":\"E43179\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw\"},{\"id\":9849008471,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity\",\"name\":\"no-issue-activity\",\"color\":\"ededed\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw\"}],\"comments\":5,\"created_at\":\"2022-03-25T08:20:22Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-05-19T02:18:08Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M5GXL0k\",\"type\":{\"id\":93574,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg\",\"name\":\"Feature\",\"description\":\"A request, idea, or new functionality\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z\"}},{\"id\":4721416566,\"number\":13471,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"CKS node Instance stuck in \\\"Starting\\\" state (VM lifecycle) when a non-default (explicitly selected) template is used; works with the default SystemVM template\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\n\\u003cp class=\\\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"39:1-43:55;1334-1737\\\"\\u003eWhen creating a CKS Kubernetes cluster and \\u003cstrong\\u003eexplicitly selecting a non-default node\\ntemplate\\u003c/strong\\u003e (the stock \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003ecks-ubuntu-2204-kvm\\u003c/code\\u003e CKS-ready image) in Advanced Settings, the\\nnode \\u003cstrong\\u003eInstance\\u003c/strong\\u003e stays in the \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eStarting\\u003c/code\\u003e \\u003cstrong\\u003eVM lifecycle state\\u003c/strong\\u003e indefinitely and never\\ntransitions to \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eRunning\\u003c/code\\u003e — even though the libvirt domain is actually up on the KVM host\\n(the VNC console is reachable and the guest OS boots).\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cp class=\\\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"45:1-49:52;1739-2127\\\"\\u003eThe same cluster creation \\u003cstrong\\u003esucceeds\\u003c/strong\\u003e when the \\u003cstrong\\u003edefault SystemVM template\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\n(\\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003esystemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64\\u003c/code\\u003e) is used for the nodes. The only changed variable between\\nthe working and failing cases is the node template selection, which points at the\\n\\u003cstrong\\u003eFlexible Kubernetes Clusters per-node template selection path\\u003c/strong\\u003e rather than at\\nin-guest provisioning (cloud-init / kubeadm / CNI).\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003ch2 class=\\\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"55:1-55:22;2375-2396\\\"\\u003eSTEPS TO REPRODUCE\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003col class=\\\"[li_\\u0026amp;]:mb-0 [li_\\u0026amp;]:mt-1 [li_\\u0026amp;]:gap-1 [\\u0026amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [\\u0026amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"57:1-68:24;2398-3079\\\"\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"57:1-57:37;2398-2434\\\"\\u003eACS 4.22.1.0 on KVM, CKS enabled.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"58:1-59:21;2435-2538\\\"\\u003eRegister the stock CKS-ready Ubuntu 22.04 KVM template (\\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003ecks-ubuntu-2204-kvm\\u003c/code\\u003e),\\nmarked \\\"For CKS\\\".\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"60:1-60:57;2539-2595\\\"\\u003eRegister a supported Kubernetes binaries ISO/version.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"61:1-63:13;2596-2780\\\"\\u003eCreate a CloudManaged Kubernetes cluster (3 control node HA) on a \\u003cstrong\\u003eVPC tier\\u003c/strong\\u003e network,\\nand in \\u003cstrong\\u003eAdvanced Settings explicitly select \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003ecks-ubuntu-2204-kvm\\u003c/code\\u003e\\u003c/strong\\u003e as the node\\ntemplate.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"64:1-65:27;2781-2886\\\"\\u003eObserve the control node Instance in the UI (Instances → the control node):\\nit stays in \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eStarting\\u003c/code\\u003e.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"66:1-68:24;2887-3079\\\"\\u003eRepeat the exact same cluster creation but \\u003cstrong\\u003edo not select a template\\u003c/strong\\u003e (use the\\ndefault \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003esystemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64\\u003c/code\\u003e): the node reaches \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eRunning\\u003c/code\\u003e and the cluster\\nprovisions normally.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ol\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003ch2 class=\\\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"70:1-70:20;3081-3100\\\"\\u003eEXPECTED RESULTS\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cp class=\\\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"72:1-75:11;3102-3367\\\"\\u003eSelecting a \\\"For CKS\\\" template in Advanced Settings should behave the same as the\\ndefault template path: the node Instance transitions \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eStarting\\u003c/code\\u003e → \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eRunning\\u003c/code\\u003e within the\\nnormal VM start window, after which CKS provisioning proceeds and the cluster reaches\\n\\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eRunning\\u003c/code\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003ch2 class=\\\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"77:1-77:18;3369-3386\\\"\\u003eACTUAL RESULTS\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cp class=\\\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"79:1-79:57;3388-3444\\\"\\u003eBehaviour depends solely on the node template selection:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cdiv class=\\\"overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"81:1-85:106;3446-3800\\\"\\u003e\\n\\nPlain Instance deployed from cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm (no CKS) | Reaches Running — works\\nCKS node from default SystemVM template systemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64 | Reaches Running, cluster provisions — works\\nCKS node from selected cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm template | Instance stuck in Starting indefinitely\\n\\n\\u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cp class=\\\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"87:1-87:21;3802-3822\\\"\\u003eIn the failing case:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cul class=\\\"[li_\\u0026amp;]:mb-0 [li_\\u0026amp;]:mt-1 [li_\\u0026amp;]:gap-1 [\\u0026amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [\\u0026amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"89:1-95:47;3824-4284\\\"\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"89:1-90:40;3824-3951\\\"\\u003eThe control node Instance remains in \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eStarting\\u003c/code\\u003e (VM lifecycle state) indefinitely, so\\nthe cluster also stays in \\u003ccode class=\\\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\\\"\\u003eStarting\\u003c/code\\u003e.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"91:1-92:26;3952-4065\\\"\\u003eThe libvirt domain is genuinely running on the KVM host: the VNC console is reachable\\nand the guest OS boots.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli class=\\\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\\\" data-sourcepos=\\\"93:1-95:47;4066-4284\\\"\\u003eSSH to the node (port 2222) is not usable; the UI-displayed password is not accepted\\non the VNC console (consistent with the node never being marked Running and/or the\\nstart/provisioning workflow not completing).\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\n### versions\\n\\nHypervisor version: KVM Ubuntu 24.04\\nACS version: 4.22.1.0\\nManagement server: Ubuntu 24.04\\n\\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### What to do about it?\\n\\n_No response_\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"akoskuczi-bw\",\"id\":158267649,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCW75AQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158267649?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/akoskuczi-bw\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/akoskuczi-bw/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":1700119912,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:kubernetes\",\"name\":\"component:kubernetes\",\"color\":\"0db7ed\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzAwMTE5OTEy\"},{\"id\":2051004353,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/distro:ubuntu\",\"name\":\"distro:ubuntu\",\"color\":\"E95420\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDUxMDA0MzUz\"}],\"comments\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-06-22T23:47:23Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-23T10:51:29Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels\",\"id\":15514689,\"number\":46,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"4.22.2\",\"description\":\"\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"sureshanaparti\",\"id\":12028987,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sureshanaparti\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":252,\"closed_issues\":114,\"created_at\":\"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T13:13:59Z\",\"node_id\":\"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABGWsZdg\",\"type\":{\"id\":93570,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFtgg\",\"name\":\"Bug\",\"description\":\"An unexpected problem or behavior\",\"color\":\"red\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-07-26T10:04:57Z\"}},{\"id\":2025868922,\"number\":8304,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Request to improve updateNetwork api \",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Improvement Request / Future request\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nAPI\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n4.18.1.0\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nRequest to improve updateNetwork api to add/change ipv6 CIRD, ipv6 gate, ipv6 end ,start ip, router ipv6. \\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nCreate ipv4 only guest network. Try to add ipv6 CIDR, gateway, start ip, end ip. \\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\nPossibility to change the settings described above using the interface or api\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\nYou won't be able to do this either through the interface or the api\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"0sorkon\",\"id\":3714094,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MTQwOTQ=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3714094?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/0sorkon\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":584073853,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:api\",\"name\":\"component:api\",\"color\":\"1DB401\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzM4NTM=\"},{\"id\":592559219,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking\",\"name\":\"component:networking\",\"color\":\"f9d0c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=\"},{\"id\":817420428,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:improvement\",\"name\":\"type:improvement\",\"color\":\"a5f9ff\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw4MTc0MjA0Mjg=\"},{\"id\":4507982790,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/ipv6\",\"name\":\"ipv6\",\"color\":\"C744C9\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABDLJbxg\"}],\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2023-12-05T10:34:13Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-29T08:12:58Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/47\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/47\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/47/labels\",\"id\":15843055,\"number\":47,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"24.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"weizhouapache\",\"id\":57355700,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MzU1NzAw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57355700?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/weizhouapache\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":272,\"closed_issues\":36,\"created_at\":\"2026-05-08T06:15:20Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T10:27:41Z\",\"node_id\":\"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A8b7v\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M54wE56\",\"type\":{\"id\":93574,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg\",\"name\":\"Feature\",\"description\":\"A request, idea, or new functionality\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z\"}},{\"id\":3449343635,\"number\":11710,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Redundant VPC VR goes dual PRIMARY (race condition?)\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\nWhen multiple network tiers are brought up in quick succession in a redundant VPC, I can consistently reproduce both VPCs going primary.\\n\\nThis is really bad because the VIP is then owned by both Virtual Routers and it means traffic is getting dropped like crazy, it makes the entire VPC unusable.  Restarting the VPC recovers it to a good state.\\n\\nPlease see the comments for debugging information, but in short it appears at least one of the nodes ends up getting munged address information which causes the wrong ips to be programmed on interfaces and the keepalived configs to diverge between nodes which causes the dual primary.  The underlying cause of the issue is this munged address information.\\n\\n### versions\\n\\n4.21.0\\n\\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\\n\\nUse Terraform to create the VPC, network tiers, and VM Instances.\\nTerraform configuration being used is here: https://github.com/bradh352/terraform-config\\n\\n\\n### What to do about it?\\n\\n_No response_\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"bradh352\",\"id\":19732188,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NzMyMTg4\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19732188?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/bradh352\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":584073391,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:virtual-router\",\"name\":\"component:virtual-router\",\"color\":\"ffaaeb\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzMzOTE=\"},{\"id\":2694797573,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-investigation\",\"name\":\"status:needs-investigation\",\"color\":\"906C28\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjk0Nzk3NTcz\"}],\"comments\":23,\"created_at\":\"2025-09-24T13:00:55Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-10T19:50:35Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels\",\"id\":15514689,\"number\":46,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"4.22.2\",\"description\":\"\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"sureshanaparti\",\"id\":12028987,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sureshanaparti\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":252,\"closed_issues\":114,\"created_at\":\"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T13:13:59Z\",\"node_id\":\"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M7NmM6T\",\"type\":{\"id\":93570,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFtgg\",\"name\":\"Bug\",\"description\":\"An unexpected problem or behavior\",\"color\":\"red\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-07-26T10:04:57Z\"}},{\"id\":3588173816,\"number\":11983,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"CS 4.20.1 Unable to run Management and secondary Storage on VXLAN - System AutoConfigures ON VLAN Untagged: the VXLAN Management and SecondaryStorage Forced to run on VLAN://untagged\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\nWe did some manual, routing corrections as a work around but want to know if this is a Bug.\\n!\\nI have the management on a vxlan, but when creating the Zone the system adds the IPs to a VLAN://untagged. that VLAN is for public.\\n!\\nThere is no way for me to move them to VXLAN the Management:\\n!\\n!\\n!\\nThe Management Interface was created during the Installation: But was loaded to a vlan://untagged - I do not have how as I specifically set for vxlan on cloudbr1\\n!\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"776\\\" height=\\\"388\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d297ee4d-6b14-4ddb-82c2-2fe4e1005a59\\\" /\\u003e\\n!\\n!\\n!\\nThe Zone Has VXLANs for Primary storage, Management, and Guest.\\n!\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"610\\\" height=\\\"412\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2115ea3-f395-4076-a4fd-69d1f9eb970c\\\" /\\u003e\\n!\\n!\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"786\\\" height=\\\"401\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6ea626b2-9106-4ae6-ad3d-f368b7a70ea6\\\" /\\u003e\\n!\\n!\\n!\\nAny Attemp to change the VLAN to VXLAN results on an error:\\n!\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"318\\\" height=\\\"94\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4adc2cab-aa97-4de4-b951-ff83360e7ef4\\\" /\\u003e\\n!\\n!\\n! Additionally The Secondary Storage is affected by this routing.\\n!\\n!\\nIs the Storage Traffic type solely for Primary storage ? I will like to have the secondary storage on a separate routed or L2/Vlan tagged\\nOur primary Storage is CEPH running on VXLAN and have no problems at all - Primary storage and Guest VXLAN are the only thing working as it should per the documentation.\\n!\\n!\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"612\\\" height=\\\"350\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d4acb42-b211-4b83-8f8a-e7fbb016c0f9\\\" /\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n### versions\\n\\nCS 4.20.1\\nPRI STORAGE:   CEPH\\nSEC STORAGE: NFS EMC\\nVXLAN\\nForced VLAN for Public - but System auto-configures the Management on vlan://untagged which also uses Secondary Storage.\\n\\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\\n\\n1. Create a new Zone, all new systems.\\n2. put on vxlan management, secondary-storage and guest on cloudbr1\\n3. pod settings: Assign the IP range for management - there is nowhere to add a VXLAN ports for Management during the initial setup/configuration\\n4. System VM proxy have to be routed manually, same as Secondary storage.\\n\\n\\nNot possible to set secondary storage using routing without VRFs, as systemVM automatically try to push it over VLAN://untagged being forced to manually route over vlan://untagged...\\n\\nAs a workaround we route sec Storage and Management over vlan://untagged\\n\\n### What to do about it?\\n\\nThe management should use the vxlan://assigend, and secondary storage should be able to have its own route if needed.\\nThe UI configures the Storage for the primary Storage only.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"tatay188\",\"id\":10108973,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTA4OTcz\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10108973?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/tatay188\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":592559219,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking\",\"name\":\"component:networking\",\"color\":\"f9d0c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=\"},{\"id\":1134705229,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:vxlan\",\"name\":\"component:vxlan\",\"color\":\"99fcc4\",\"description\":\"VXLAN\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTM0NzA1MjI5\"},{\"id\":1150675549,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature\",\"name\":\"type:new-feature\",\"color\":\"4471c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5\"}],\"comments\":11,\"created_at\":\"2025-11-04T21:15:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-01T14:21:09Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M7V3y_4\",\"type\":{\"id\":93574,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg\",\"name\":\"Feature\",\"description\":\"A request, idea, or new functionality\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z\"}},{\"id\":766468471,\"number\":4542,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Reserve IP address for out of bounds machines\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and master branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nAbility to define IP address beside of choosing VMs in Static NAT, Port Forward and Load balancer services to provide those services to servers outside of CloudStack.\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Feature Idea\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nVR\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on master branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nAll versions\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nAdvanced networking\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nIn some network services we need to specify which VM should use it. For example Static NAT, Port Forward and Load balancer.\\r\\nIt would be a good idea if we can also specify IP address of a server which is not managed by CloudStack.\\r\\nThis feature helps us to use network services provided by virtual router for physical servers or even VMs outside of CloudStack management area but share a common L2 network with other VMs in CloudStack.\\r\\nThis feature also requires reserve IP address capability in all type of networks. We can expand the issue #4357 for private IPs in isolated networks too.\\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Create an isolated network\\r\\n2. In Port forward section define a new rule\\r\\n3. In \\\"Add VM\\\" panel write IP address of the server outside of CloudStack\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\nAn iptables rule created in virtual router to forward desired port to the server IP\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\nIt is not possible to mention IP address of the server outside of CloudStack\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"aleskxyz\",\"id\":39186039,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MTg2MDM5\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39186039?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/aleskxyz\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aleskxyz/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":592559219,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking\",\"name\":\"component:networking\",\"color\":\"f9d0c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=\"},{\"id\":2249631279,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:experimental-feature\",\"name\":\"type:experimental-feature\",\"color\":\"c1fca4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwyMjQ5NjMxMjc5\"},{\"id\":2531618875,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/complexity:simple\",\"name\":\"complexity:simple\",\"color\":\"000088\",\"description\":\"a few days to a couple of weeks\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwyNTMxNjE4ODc1\"},{\"id\":9851088157,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/long-term-plan\",\"name\":\"long-term-plan\",\"color\":\"aaaaaa\",\"description\":\"remove this label if you plan to pick up this issue.\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSyutHQ\"}],\"comments\":26,\"created_at\":\"2020-12-14T13:58:37Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-25T06:46:30Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"parent_issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9958\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"MDU6SXNzdWU3NjY0Njg0NzE=\",\"type\":{\"id\":93574,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg\",\"name\":\"Feature\",\"description\":\"A request, idea, or new functionality\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z\"}},{\"id\":1681234383,\"number\":7458,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"ACS doesn't let me create isolated networks with ranges which are not RFC1918\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Bug Report\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nAPI, UI, logic\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n4.18\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nKVM with Tungsten Fabric\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\nI want to create an isolated network with Public IPs which will be then routed with a Tungsten Logical Router.\\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n-\\u003e Add Network, Isolated. In Gateway place a non-RFC1918 range.\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nFor the network to be created with that range\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\\"Virtual Guest Cidr 33.65.45.0/24 is not RFC 1918 or 6598 compliant\\\"\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"alexandremattioli\",\"id\":60507727,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTA3NzI3\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60507727?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/alexandremattioli\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/alexandremattioli/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":5426531036,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:tungsten-fabric\",\"name\":\"component:tungsten-fabric\",\"color\":\"F313C4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABQ3JK3A\"},{\"id\":6890295339,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale\",\"name\":\"status:stale\",\"color\":\"E43179\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw\"},{\"id\":9849008471,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity\",\"name\":\"no-issue-activity\",\"color\":\"ededed\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw\"}],\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2023-04-24T13:04:04Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-06T02:17:37Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/7458\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/7458\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/7458/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/7458/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/7458/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/7458/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M5kNZnP\"},{\"id\":1431841155,\"number\":6861,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"VM Password reset - Unable to set Password Complexity requirement for Special Characters\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Bug Report\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nUI\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n4.17.0\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nUnable to Set Password Complexity requirement to include special characters \\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nOur organization wants to enforce password requirements upon password resets on the VM. The default password requirement is 6 characters. I have updated that to 14 characters using vm.password.length\\r\\n\\r\\nHowever, there is no provision to enforce inclusion of select special characters (like !@#%^\\u0026*()-) -- exclude the $\\r\\n\\r\\nIs there some way to achieve this? \\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nOur organization wants to enforce password requirements upon password resets on the VM. The default password requirement is 6 characters. I have updated that to 14 characters using vm.password.length\\r\\n\\r\\nHowever, there is no provision to enforce inclusion of select special characters (like !@#%^\\u0026*()-) -- exclude the $\\r\\n\\r\\nIs there some way to achieve this? \\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nPassword reset only includes numbers, upper and lower case\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"nxsbi\",\"id\":71042351,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMDQyMzUx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71042351?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/nxsbi\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":1150675549,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature\",\"name\":\"type:new-feature\",\"color\":\"4471c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5\"},{\"id\":6890295339,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale\",\"name\":\"status:stale\",\"color\":\"E43179\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw\"},{\"id\":9849008471,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity\",\"name\":\"no-issue-activity\",\"color\":\"ededed\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw\"}],\"comments\":26,\"created_at\":\"2022-11-01T17:57:01Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-05-27T02:18:38Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M5VWCmD\"},{\"id\":2531348246,\"number\":9693,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"No. of CPU Cores in Compute Cluster doesnt display correctly when Cluster has oversubscription more than 1\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Bug Report\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nCompute Cluster UI\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n4.19.1.1\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have 2 Compute Clusters:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Cluster 1 : Oversubcription = 1\\r\\n- Cluster 2 : Oversubcription = 2\\r\\n\\r\\nRefering to the screenshot below, Cluster 1 is showing the correct No. of CPU Cores allocated. \\r\\n\\r\\nBut for Cluster 2, it seems inaccurate. The number of allocation exceeded whats available. Resulting in a UI error. \\r\\n\\r\\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 23 55 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/36c46ff6-7d2a-4641-80e5-48e28e040ad0)\\r\\n\\r\\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 24 05 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68972682-4bf4-41d4-8d4e-d61b82132c35)\\r\\n\\r\\nBut the bigger problem now, is that both clusters have exceeded the allocation threshold, but there was no notification sent. And neither did cloudstack stop users from creating new virtual machines from the clusters.\\r\\n\\r\\nWithout this, Admins would not be able to ensure n+1 sufficient capacity in the event of a node failure. \\r\\n\\r\\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 34 14 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/550f0ab7-dc3b-4fbf-b757-75153761b17c)\\r\\n\\r\\nIn summary, there are 3 Issues:\\r\\n\\r\\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should display the full available amount, after oversubscription\\r\\n- Admin should get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\\r\\n- User should not be able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should display the full available amount, after oversubscription\\r\\n- Admin should get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\\r\\n- User should not be able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should not displaying total available cores correctly, after oversubscription.\\r\\n- Admin did not get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\\r\\n- User is able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"btzq\",\"id\":147712084,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCM3oVA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147712084?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/btzq\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":2630836378,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-functional-definition\",\"name\":\"status:needs-functional-definition\",\"color\":\"951862\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjMwODM2Mzc4\"}],\"comments\":12,\"created_at\":\"2024-09-17T14:38:58Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-07T01:45:36Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M6W4U8W\"},{\"id\":1565844175,\"number\":7155,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"tests should only run when applicable for adv-sg zone in such env\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Documentation Report\\r\\n * testing/CI\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nmarvin\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n4.18\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nadvanced zone with security groups.\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\nwhen an advanced zone with security groups is used to test for regressions, a lot of errors occur.\\r\\nan example\\r\\n```\\r\\nERROR: test suite for \\u003cclass 'tests.smoke.test_router_dns.TestRouterDns'\\u003e\\r\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\r\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/nose/suite.py\\\", line 210, in run\\r\\n    self.setUp()\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/nose/suite.py\\\", line 293, in setUp\\r\\n    self.setupContext(ancestor)\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/nose/suite.py\\\", line 316, in setupContext\\r\\n    try_run(context, names)\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/nose/util.py\\\", line 471, in try_run\\r\\n    return func()\\r\\n  File \\\"/marvin/tests/smoke/test_router_dns.py\\\", line 92, in setUpClass\\r\\n    zoneid=cls.zone.id)\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/lib/base.py\\\", line 3562, in create\\r\\n    return Network(apiclient.createNetwork(cmd).__dict__)\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/cloudstackAPI/cloudstackAPIClient.py\\\", line 2981, in createNetwork\\r\\n    response = self.connection.marvinRequest(command, response_type=response, method=method)\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/cloudstackConnection.py\\\", line 381, in marvinRequest\\r\\n    raise e\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/cloudstackConnection.py\\\", line 376, in marvinRequest\\r\\n    raise self.__lastError\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/cloudstackConnection.py\\\", line 310, in __parseAndGetResponse\\r\\n    response_cls)\\r\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/jsonHelper.py\\\", line 155, in getResultObj\\r\\n    raise cloudstackException.CloudstackAPIException(respname, errMsg)\\r\\nmarvin.cloudstackException.CloudstackAPIException: Execute cmd: createnetwork failed, due to: errorCode: 431, errorText:Only shared guest network can be created in security group enabled zone\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nthis is not necessary as we know beforehand that these tests will fail.\\r\\nTests need to be properly tagged to not run in these environments.\\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\ntest will not run\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\ntest runs and fails\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":37843366,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:enhancement\",\"name\":\"type:enhancement\",\"color\":\"84b6eb\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2Ng==\"},{\"id\":9851088157,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/long-term-plan\",\