-04-13T07:02:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T13:13:59Z\",\"node_id\":\"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/7961/reactions\"},\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"weizhouapache\",\"id\":57355700,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MzU1NzAw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57355700?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/weizhouapache\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M5w5prc\",\"type\":{\"id\":93570,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFtgg\",\"name\":\"Bug\",\"description\":\"An unexpected problem or behavior\",\"color\":\"red\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-07-26T10:04:57Z\"}},{\"id\":2028308883,\"number\":8314,\"state\":\"closed\",\"state_reason\":\"completed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"IPv6 does not work\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Bug Report\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nNetwork\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n4.18.1.0\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nAdvanced network, isolated network with dualstack ip config\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nCompute:\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nroot@cloud2:~# cat /etc/os-release\\r\\nPRETTY_NAME=\\\"Ubuntu 22.04.3 LTS\\\"\\r\\nNAME=\\\"Ubuntu\\\"\\r\\nVERSION_ID=\\\"22.04\\\"\\r\\nVERSION=\\\"22.04.3 LTS (Jammy Jellyfish)\\\"\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\nWhen creating an isolated network with ipv4+ipv6, ip addresses are assigned to the VM (displayed in the interface), but are not received via DHCP from the virtual router inside VM. At the same time ipv4 addresses are received by guest VMs normally. Setting the enable-ra option, which is not enabled by default in /etc/dnsmasq.conf has no effect. When assigning ipv6 manually to the guest VM (the one specified in the interface), ping to the virtual router fails with the error \\r\\n~~~\\r\\nDestination unreachable: Address unreachable. \\r\\n~~~\\r\\ntcpdump on the bridge where virtual interfaces are located:\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n12:03:15.186417 IP6 2a00:1728:23:109f:1:ff:fee7:1 \\u003e ff02::1:ff00:1: ICMP6, neighbor solicitation, who has 2a00:1728:23:109f::1, length 32\\r\\n12:03:16.210411 IP6 2a00:1728:23:109f:1:ff:fee7:1 \\u003e ff02::1:ff00:1: ICMP6, neighbor solicitation, who has 2a00:1728:23:109f::1, length 32\\r\\n12:03:17.234483 IP6 2a00:1728:23:109f:1:ff:fee7:1 \\u003e ff02::1:ff00:1: ICMP6, neighbor solicitation, who has 2a00:1728:23:109f::1, length 32\\r\\n12:03:17.234737 IP 10.1.1.254.22 \\u003e 10.1.1.1.59366: Flags [P.], seq 1169432167:1169432483, ack 3282011073, win 501, length 316\\r\\n12:03:17.234945 IP 10.1.1.1.59366 \\u003e 10.1.1.254.22: Flags [.], ack 316, win 5882, length 0\\r\\n12:03:18.258392 IP6 2a00:1728:23:109f:1:ff:fee7:1 \\u003e ff02::1:ff00:1: ICMP6, neighbor solicitation, who has 2a00:1728:23:109f::1, length 32\\r\\n12:03:18.410325 IP6 fe80::1:ff:fee7:2 \\u003e ff02::1: ICMP6, router advertisement, length 104\\r\\n12:03:19.282398 IP6 2a00:1728:23:109f:1:ff:fee7:1 \\u003e ff02::1:ff00:1: ICMP6, neighbor solicitation, who has 2a00:1728:23:109f::1, length 32\\r\\n12:03:20.306561 IP6 2a00:1728:23:109f:1:ff:fee7:1 \\u003e ff02::1:ff00:1: ICMP6, neighbor solicitation, who has 2a00:1728:23:109f::1, length 32\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nTested on Debian 11, Ubuntu 22.04 b CentOS5 (deployed from built-in template). No additional configurations at host level.\\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\ncreate an isolated network as shown in the video https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rqqJENCAwoo. Create a VM on this network. Log in to the VM and check the ipv6 assignment on the primary interface. Try pinging the virtual router\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\nGuest VM gets ipv6 by dhcp and can ping the virtual router\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\nGuest VM does not get ipv6 ip over dhcp and cannot ping the virtual router\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"0sorkon\",\"id\":3714094,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MTQwOTQ=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3714094?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/0sorkon\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":37843366,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:enhancement\",\"name\":\"type:enhancement\",\"color\":\"84b6eb\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2Ng==\"},{\"id\":584073336,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:ipv6\",\"name\":\"component:ipv6\",\"color\":\"c2e0c6\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzMzMzY=\"},{\"id\":592559219,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking\",\"name\":\"component:networking\",\"color\":\"f9d0c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node